{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"9fd7c166fa16791dba4ea50378f2f4dd5eba2367bba08b579e44fbac8a7af1b1","occurred_at":"2026-11-21T23:35:15Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[99,102]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-live-binding.py","quoted_text":"DEPENDENCY_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?P<directive>Wants|Requires|Requisite|BindsTo|PartOf|Conflicts|\"\n    r\"WantedBy|RequiredBy|Also|Upholds|OnFailure|OnSuccess|Triggers|\"\n    r\"TriggersBy|Unit|Service)\\s*=\\s*(?P<value>.*)\")","reason":"The regex is the dependency-scan directive set. Systemd v257 adds `PropagatesStopTo=`/`StopPropagatedFrom=` as [Unit] dependency directives creating an inverse stop binding: a co-installed unit can stop the selected unit without discovery seeing the relationship, so `supported=True` can be reported incorrectly. Adding both to the existing alternation is a minimal correctness fix, not a new requirement.","target":"a64095ef5d2972c8c40e28cb25ed76d1799d3c66"},"finding_id":"1d6d3a879edaf2afe7e9a329fb5916c084c5d2f4f230f484983ff91ea4a44881","previous_event_id":"2e65c8c7ccea5c4e8f4e8571c008cff98b08cfbc5a8965358a3fbe4218b3de0a","review_id":"9a9770d007f4898ae9f169624c7b761856e1e349d118670986a85a8250d506cd"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:1d6d3a879edaf2afe7e9a329fb5916c084c5d2f4f230f484983ff91ea4a44881:3cd7025a3baf79f8b8342674439fc5061d2c2027a59474bc95c8d180cdbc90a0"}